# Cloudflare asset headers. Vite copies this file into dist/ at build time, and
# the Hercules publish pipeline hands it to Cloudflare as the app's asset config.
#
# Why this file has to exist: Cloudflare's asset runtime ships exactly one
# built-in Cache-Control -- "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate" -- and applies
# it to every file, whether or not the name is content-hashed. Neither Wrangler
# nor @cloudflare/vite-plugin generates a default to override it, so a _headers
# file is the only supported way to change it.
#
# Without the rule below, a returning visitor revalidates every script,
# stylesheet and font before the page can render. Each one is a blocking round
# trip to the edge that ends in a 304 with an empty body.
#
# Vite fingerprints everything it emits into /assets, so the bytes behind a
# given URL never change -- a rebuild produces a new filename instead. That
# makes them safe to pin for a year and mark immutable, which also stops the
# browser revalidating them on a manual reload.
#
# index.html is deliberately left alone: it keeps the must-revalidate default so
# a new deploy is picked up on the next navigation.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
